{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080113-monster-themed-legacies","id":1080113,"title":"Monster themed legacies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-17T18:15:09-07:00","id":1080113,"title":"Monster themed legacies","content":"Unfortunately i don't know much about legacy design but i was wondering how hard it would be to create themed legacies for mages based around the other templates. For example a wolf blooded thrysus who wanted to call on aspects of being a werewolf as legacy attainments, or a ghoul who wanted to tap the power of vampire blood for attainments powered by vitae. It just seems like it would be a good way of working a mage into a crossover is to have them fit the theme of the main group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T05:49:06-07:00","id":1080267,"title":"","content":"So,mechanics-wise i don't think it would be that different from any other legacy. Choose an arcanum that fits the splat (spirit/life for werewolves, death for vampires) and choose some attainments that fit that creature's power and that's most done already. <br /> <br /> Fluffwise- it's unclear if Mage can be wolf-blooded or ghouls, but discarding that you are reshaping your soul to be more like that of a supernatural creature. That probably has some side effects, but unless it is covered in the Crossover Chronicle, it is mostly up to the ST what precisely those effects are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T05:58:49-07:00","id":1080274,"title":"","content":"A Mage can be a wolf-blooded. 'Unless she goes through the First Change, a Wolf-Blooded character retains her Tell if she becomes another kind of supernatural creature.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T06:17:22-07:00","id":1080283,"title":"","content":"Fair enough!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T02:18:16-07:00","id":1087583,"title":"","content":"I've always assumed a Mage could be ghouled, since they wouldn't seem to have any particular immunity to it. From a narrative point of view it would be interesting to have a ghouled mage develop the Legacy to be more like their master, and then have the bond lapse, leading to a lot of resentment over the now-unwanted Legacy.<br /> <br /> It's also worth considering that the Attainments wouldn't have to really mirror the powers of the other type, but could be built upon the themes or symbolic nature of the other creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1547-bunnirabbi","name":"BunniRabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1547_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T04:20:55-07:00","id":1087617,"title":"","content":"*considers* I could totally see a Death themed Mastigos Vampire Legacy that recreated the blood bond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T10:17:41-07:00","id":1087777,"title":"","content":"I did something like that for a friend of mine.<br /> <br /> Thyrsus Legacy focused on Werewolf.<br /> Primary Arcana: Life<br /> Optional Arcana: Spirit<br /> <br /> I'll look it up and post it as soon as I find it.<br /> And I'm also thinking about a Vampire themed one. But Moros or Mastigos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T10:24:09-07:00","id":1087780,"title":"","content":"Might I suggest <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1078825\">Thyrsus</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T11:18:48-07:00","id":1087814,"title":"","content":"About the Werewolf one, here is the basic:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">1st and 2nd Attainments are basic for Wolf Senses.<br /> <br /> 1st: Analyze Life (Life 1). Reach for Instant Activation<br /> Op: Know Spirit (Spirit 1). Reach for Instant Activation<br /> <br /> 2nd: Heightened Senses (Life 1). Reach for Instant Activation and Increased Duration.<br /> Op: Exorcist\u2019s Eye (Spirit 1). Reach for Instant Activation and Increased Duration<br /> <br /> 3rd, 4th and 5th Attainments are for Wolfing around, healing, crossing the gauntlet and stuff.<br /> <br /> 3rd: Transform Life (Life 3). Atypical duration, you can maintain this form for Advanced Duration, despite it's Reach being on Instant Activation.<br /> It's the werewolf form, with +1 size, Claws and Leaping. When the mage gets more Life he can further enhance his wolf form.<br /> The Atypical part is that you enter on a kind of Frenesi after spending more than Stamina+Gnosis turns transformed in a given Scene, and you need 3 sucesses on a Resolve+Composure to revert to your human form.<br /> Op: Gossamer Touch (Spirit 2). Reach for Instant Activation and Increased Duration<br /> <br /> 4th: Mend (Life 4). Reach for Instant Activation (Cause we like heals)<br /> Op: Reaching (Spirit 3) Reach for Instant Activation and for opening Irises.<br /> <br /> 5th: Shapechanging (Life 4) Reach for Instant Activation and Increased Duration.<br /> Op: Shadow Scream (Spirit 4) Reach for Instant Activation and Aggravated Damage.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080113-monster-themed-legacies?p=1087780#post1087780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might I suggest <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1078825\">Thyrsus</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about the ability that Strix have for harvesting Vitae from the act of breathing, I tried to analyse the Vitae. After reading About Vitae (Vampire 2ed p. 98) and Vitae Addiction (p. 99) I came to the conclusion that it is probably Life and Death. Cause it's a product of a Vampire stealing the Life from a target and turning it into Vitae because of his Curse. I'm assuming that the Curse is a part of the nature of Vampire Souls. It's probably easier to make it using Life and Death as Arcanas. So, Moros or Thyrsus, depending on whats the optional Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 05-04-2017, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T11:23:55-07:00","id":1087816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080113-monster-themed-legacies?p=1087814#post1087814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the Werewolf one, here is the basic:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">1st and 2nd Attainments are basic for Wolf Senses.<br /> <br /> 1st: Analyze Life (Life 1). Reach for Instant Activation<br /> Op: Know Spirit (Spirit 1). Reach for Instant Activation<br /> <br /> 2nd: Heightened Senses (Life 1). Reach for Instant Activation and Increased Duration.<br /> Op: Exorcist\u2019s Eye (Spirit 1). Reach for Instant Activation and Increased Duration<br /> <br /> 3rd, 4th and 5th Attainments are for Wolfing around, healing, crossing the gauntlet and stuff.<br /> <br /> 3rd: Transform Life (Life 3). Atypical duration, you can maintain this form for Advanced Duration, despite it's Reach being on Instant Activation.<br /> It's the werewolf form, with +1 size, Claws and Leaping. When the mage gets more Life he can further enhance his wolf form.<br /> The Atypical part is that you enter on a kind of Frenesi after spending more than Stamina+Gnosis turns transformed in a given Scene, and you need 3 sucesses on a Resolve+Composure to revert to your human form.<br /> Op: Gossamer Touch (Spirit 2). Reach for Instant Activation and Increased Duration<br /> <br /> 4th: Mend (Life 4). Reach for Instant Activation (Cause we like heals)<br /> Op: Reaching (Spirit 3) Reach for Instant Activation and for opening Irises.<br /> <br /> 5th: Shapechanging (Life 4) Reach for Instant Activation and Increased Duration.<br /> Op: Shadow Scream (Spirit 4) Reach for Instant Activation and Aggravated Damage.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thinking about the ability that Strix have for harvesting Vitae from the act of breathing, I tried to analyse the Vitae. After reading About Vitae (Vampire 2ed p. 98) and Vitae Addiction (p. 99) I came to the conclusion that it is probably Life and Death. Cause it's a product of a Vampire stealing the Life from a target and turning it into Vitae because of his Curse. I'm assuming that the Curse is a part of the nature of Vampire Souls. It's probably easier to make it using Life and Death as Arcanas. So, Moros or Thyrsus, depending on whats the optional Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a heads up the spells used for the first attainment require the spell to be cast on a target, not the Mage. Currently you'd have to touch your subject or use it as an Aimed effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T11:31:12-07:00","id":1087823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080113-monster-themed-legacies?p=1087816#post1087816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just a heads up the spells used for the first attainment require the spell to be cast on a target, not the Mage. Currently you'd have to touch your subject or use it as an Aimed effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he got this power to work by sniffing close(almost touching) to the target. We did it cause it sounded kinda funny and he wanted to do it that way.<br /> <br /> Edit: By &quot;he&quot;, I mean the friend that I helped with the development of the Legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T12:11:34-07:00","id":1087841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080113-monster-themed-legacies?p=1087814#post1087814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about the ability that Strix have for harvesting Vitae from the act of breathing, I tried to analyse the Vitae. After reading About Vitae (Vampire 2ed p. 98) and Vitae Addiction (p. 99) I came to the conclusion that it is probably Life and Death. Cause it's a product of a Vampire stealing the Life from a target and turning it into Vitae because of his Curse. I'm assuming that the Curse is a part of the nature of Vampire Souls. It's probably easier to make it using Life and Death as Arcanas. So, Moros or Thyrsus, depending on whats the optional Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's more explicable than thematic. IMO Life and Mind seem more linked to Vampire's themes. Just because you're undead, doesn't mean you need to focus on the Death Arcanum.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T12:17:02-07:00","id":1087845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080113-monster-themed-legacies?p=1087841#post1087841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's more explicable than thematic. IMO Life and Mind seem more linked to Vampire's themes. Just because you're undead, doesn't mean you need to focus on the Death Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Death kind of has a vampire thing going on already though if you squint a bit, Death Mage Armor downgrades damage, Devouring the Slain, etc. Also undeath basically falls under its purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-04-2017, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T12:22:43-07:00","id":1087851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080113-monster-themed-legacies?p=1087845#post1087845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Death kind of has a vampire thing going on already though if you squint a bit, Death Mage Armor downgrades damage, Devouring the Slain, etc. Also undeath basically falls under its purview.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good point. I think I'd still go with Mind over Life though because of the sheer number of mind-affecting powers that Vampires have (Majesty, Nightmare, Dominate, Auspex (after-a-fashion)).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T13:32:53-07:00","id":1087892,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd agree with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T21:09:44-07:00","id":1088094,"title":"","content":"Something that I've spent some time thinking about but never really gotten anywhere with is the idea of a nameless order/legacy that has developed an enshrined role in a non-mage supernatural society. For instance, maybe in a specific protectorate (like, in California, perhaps) it is traditional for packs to have an awakened advisor, whose presence grants the pack extra legitimacy in the eyes of that particular society. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}